{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Come</b> — Because He mentioned that He is King, therefore we are obligated to bow down before Him." "<b>Let us bless</b> — Like ויברך על ברכיו (and he kneeled upon his knees)." "<b>And the meaning of our Maker</b> — For He made the sea and the dry land, and they are universals, and from them He made the particulars."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 95, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:20.128539254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}